Z||000016||william_thorniii||02-01-2001||09:50 AM||||Gentlemen,<P>The fact of the matter is that Eddie has sold the molds (last summer).  He was only asking $10-15,000 at that point.  This is an extremely low price considering folks pay $1000+ for PISA dashes and the like.  Part of the agreement was that the purchaser must make interior kits available for sale.  I helped Eddy communicate with Mr. Tilden prior to the sale (since Eddy's English is not his strong point).  At that time Mr. Tilden claimed that his neighbor was going to make them for him.  I am not aware if Eddy placed a statute of limitations on the time that Mr. Tilden had before Eddy would make his back up molds available.   <P>If and only if Mr. Tilden does not get kits to the market, then Eddy will consider selling his back up set of molds.  They are the wood molds that are shown on his website.  <P>Like many of you, I would kill to have an interior that looked like Eddys.  It is near perfect. <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||13
Z||000017||TwisT||02-01-2001||02:12 PM||||William,<P>On behalf of all of us Fiero owner's who have been seeking information about Eddy's kit,  I would like to thank you for providing us with great information.  I know that Eddy is very proud of his interior,  and I know that he is concerned about getting the molds to someone who will in fact reproduce and sell kits faithfully.<P>Eddy's one hell of a guy...  I spoke to him a couple of years ago about his interior when it wasn't even finished.  He even asked me if I was interested in purchasing the molds for reproduction (!!!!!) when he was finished with them.  At the time,  I believe he was talking with Mr. Mike's about it.  I always thought that Mr. Mike would have been a shoe-in candidate for Eddy's interior,  but I'm not sure exactly why he didn't take it on.<P>William,  if you can,  let Eddy know that he's got a lot of Pennock (and non=Pennock) Fiero enthusiasts feeling that his interior is the best we've seen.<P>For those of you who haven't visited Eddy's Fiero page,  here is his link:<P> <A HREF="http://members.tripod.lycos.nl/FIERO_2/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.lycos.nl/FIERO_2/index.html</A> <P><BR>Thanks again William!  Oh yeah,  don't forget to get Eddy to join Pennock,  even if his English isn't that great!<P>Brett <P>'88 "ITALFIERO" GT<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||BAM-BAM||02-03-2001||10:54 AM|||| I saw this kit for sale on E-Bay a couple of months ago. This same picture was featured. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tildeninterior.jpg"> <BR> I can't recall the details. I know that I downloaded the pic for some reason. Then I went to the link posted above and there it was. I think someone should contact "Mr" Tilden and find out what's going on. If anyone has his E-Mail addy, I'll do it. LMK<P> Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 02-03-2001).]||||reg||8
